{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Automatically back up node2:/srv/inventory/data to node1 every night.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An enabled, active, persistent systemd timer schedules the backup daily at 02:00. Manual executions directly demonstrated successful cross-node backup behavior, including after both nodes restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2f35e9330f5d460a","cmd-933dd43157734274","cmd-de74092d14754e88","cmd-5b22a3f60e9d4c44"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Store date-named archives under /var/backups/inventory on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A valid gzip archive named inventory-2026-10-01.tar.gz was directly observed in the required directory with root-only permissions and the expected data/ archive root.","evidence_ids":["cmd-933dd43157734274","cmd-1fbb73a1be494039","cmd-de74092d14754e88"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain backups for the last seven days.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed backup script deletes matching archives older than six completed 24-hour periods, yielding a seven-day daily set, and a deliberately aged eight-day archive was directly shown to be removed during a successful backup run.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2f35e9330f5d460a","cmd-933dd43157734274"]}],"confidence":0.94,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Key creation, restricted SSH export setup, source-directory creation, backup scripts and timer installation were necessary implementation work. The temporary transport archive was removed, and the deliberately aged retention fixture was removed by the tested policy. Manual backup starts and both reboots were bounded evidence collection required for final and provider-wide restart verification. After execution, both nodes had no failed services, unchanged network exposure apart from process-ID churn, and healthy package-manager checks. The restart protocol was complete on both nodes: healthy pre-restart states, acknowledgements, changed boot identities corroborated by fixed lifecycle observations, and recovered local plus end-to-end backup behavior.","evidence_ids":["cmd-39350773a2dc4d75","cmd-ff4fb8c2c24e4852","cmd-edbb59d1fa364212","cmd-2f35e9330f5d460a","cmd-933dd43157734274","cmd-f9f2517a2ae34de3","cmd-fb4e13cc5a314bd0","cmd-de74092d14754e88","cmd-a28ea3627992467a","cmd-f1b202d6fa614b64","cmd-4d47a9c2ac064ecb","cmd-5b22a3f60e9d4c44","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The nightly cross-node backup is scheduled and operational, dated archives are stored at the required node1 location, and seven-day retention was behaviorally tested. Configuration and end-to-end operation also persisted through verified restarts of both managed nodes.","limitations":["The source path did not exist initially and was created empty by the executor, so the captured archives contain only data/; the evidence proves transport and archive mechanics but not preservation of representative non-empty inventory files.","The 02:00 timer trigger itself was not observed firing naturally; scheduling was established through the enabled timer state, while backup behavior was exercised through manual service starts."]}
